# Coding Standards

Keep backend code uniform, reusable, and reviewable.

## Requirements
- CommonJS only.
- Module folders use kebab-case; functions use camelCase; constants use `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`.
- Database, Prisma model, schema, migration, and documented payload fields use lowercase `snake_case`.
- Prefer small reusable services and helpers over copy-paste implementations.
- Public functions, exported modules, and complex logic must have JSDoc-style comments.
- Inline comments must explain intent, assumptions, or edge cases only.
- Do not read `process.env` outside config helpers.
- Do not hardcode authorization, entitlement, or role logic in controllers.
- Do not add duplicate helper libraries when an existing family can be extended.
- Circular dependencies, dead files, and stale comments are defects.
